#X msg 590 1040 setB scenes 0 sirens 0 mode play;
#X msg 860 1040 setB scenes 1 sceneName montee;
#X msg 1090 1040 build;
#X obj 20 1080 print pdjson-setB;
#X text 20 1110 numeric path elements are 0-based array indices -- scenes 0 then scenes 1 therefore build a two-element ARRAY of objects. <key...> <value> is exactly the shape dump outputs\, so the dump of another pdjson can be piped straight back into setB with no translation -- that is what it is for. Unlike set\, setB writes into the builder (what build serialises)\, not into the loaded json_data\, and does no deepcopy: it is meant to be called once per dump line.;
#X text 20 1230 pushArray -- append a NEW object to an array and descend into it (2026-07-17);
#X obj 20 1290 pdjson;
#X msg 20 1320 clearBuilder;
#X msg 130 1320 pushArray states;
#X msg 290 1320 add siren 1;
#X msg 420 1320 pop;
#X msg 490 1320 pushArray states;
#X msg 650 1320 add siren 2;
#X msg 780 1320 pop;
#X msg 850 1320 build;
#X obj 20 1360 print pdjson-pushArray;
#X text 20 1390 push alone re-enters the SAME object at that key every time\, so it cannot build a list of distinct elements -- pushArray appends a fresh one and descends into it. Repeat pushArray / add... / pop once per element.;
